# The runtime environment of the GC stress workflow's "concurrent" build (.github/workflows/gc-stress.yml): Mono's
# concurrent mark-and-sweep collector, which TabStudio turned off (AndroidEnableSGenConcurrent in
# src/TabStudio.Android/TabStudio.Android.csproj), checking its own invariants. It reproduces the runtime race that
# made TabStudio abort in the collector: SIGSEGV or SIGBUS on the SGen worker thread, an array freed while in use,
# or one of SGen's own assertions. Run it to see whether a new .NET runtime has fixed the race; until then this
# build is expected to crash in some of its runs.
#
# Build it yourself with:
#   dotnet publish src/TabStudio.Android -c Release -f net10.0-android -p:TabStudioAndroidEnvironment=build/android/gc-stress/concurrent.env
#
# A 1 MB nursery (the default is 4 MB) makes minor collections, and with them the bridge's walks during a
# concurrent mark, four times as frequent.
MONO_GC_PARAMS=major=marksweep-conc,nursery-size=1m

# check-concurrent  checks the nursery around every concurrent collection, and clears it at each one.
# clear-at-gc       clears the nursery at each collection, so a stale pointer reads zeros.
# Two checks cannot run with the concurrent collector. check-mark-bits: building the nursery's fragments clears the
# pins just before it asserts that everything left in the nursery is pinned, so it aborts at the first major
# collection. mod-union-consistency-check: it runs when a concurrent collection is made to finish early, after the
# workers stopped with marked objects still waiting to be scanned, whose references then count as missing from the
# mod-union cards ("major->major reference ... not found in remsets") although nothing was lost.
MONO_GC_DEBUG=check-concurrent,clear-at-gc
